{"timestamp":"2026-10-01T16:07:58.249Z","level":"info","event":"provider.together.response","fields":{"provider":"together","endpoint":"/chat/completions","response":{"httpStatus":200,"contentType":"text/event-stream","providerRequestId":"5d80f3b8-aws_ec1","model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","text":"{\"schemaVersion\":\"objectives-v2\",\"objectives\":[{\"statement\":\"Explain how Proverbs 8:18-21 links enduring riches and honor with walking in righteousness and justice, and how this promise frames the believer's approach to wealth.\",\"verb\":\"explain\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"8002a06a-c3ea-73c3-a83e-4caa9d2ccbc3\",\"43234e5f-2cdc-73bf-9a4a-095f64dbcf9d\"],\"confidence\":0.95},{\"statement\":\"Compare the two manifestations of righteousness—the gift received by grace through faith and the harvest of righteousness that grows through visible works—and analyze how the David analogy distinguishes standing in faith before God from showing works before people.\",\"verb\":\"compare\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"8324c242-533b-726a-9458-03cf5d83458a\",\"edf97ec5-6993-78af-8f09-fc6f0892a758\",\"a62601c8-062f-7006-b0ca-b4c236e7ea47\",\"fb4cfa61-881b-78f2-8173-853f0e169c5b\"],\"confidence\":0.95},{\"statement\":\"Describe generosity as a willing overflow of spiritual righteousness rather than forced compliance, distinguishing a cheerful bountiful sower from one who sows sparingly out of reluctant compulsion.\",\"verb\":\"describe\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"66522a60-bc03-7abf-8434-23545728a3ae\"],\"confidence\":0.92},{\"statement\":\"Analyze the Hebrew concept of Tzedakah by identifying its three ramifications—personal morality, justice, and charity—and evaluate how this fused understanding reframes giving to the poor as a matter of justice rather than optional benevolence.\",\"verb\":\"analyse\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"ca763446-f8c9-7a62-b9c7-2a09335682b3\",\"ac2e0a05-29b4-74c8-a832-f25b79a51268\",\"168b403a-2303-7e1a-ae75-b2ebe56da6b2\",\"0f6e5794-b307-734e-83ba-78fb071fdb2c\"],\"confidence\":0.94},{\"statement\":\"Identify the consecrated financial laws of Kingdom economics—fairness over legal rights, periodic debt cancellation, leaving gleanings, prompt payment of workers, and refusing to exploit desperation—and explain how they contradict self-serving worldly models.\",\"verb\":\"identify\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"564578eb-71d4-7e3e-8488-3848c22e28c8\",\"18fc39b0-81c3-7","textChunks":["{\"schemaVersion\":\"objectives-v2\",\"objectives\":[{\"statement\":\"Explain how Proverbs 8:18-21 links enduring riches and honor with walking in righteousness and justice, and how this promise frames the believer's approach to wealth.\",\"verb\":\"explain\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"8002a06a-c3ea-73c3-a83e-4caa9d2ccbc3\",\"43234e5f-2cdc-73bf-9a4a-095f64dbcf9d\"],\"confidence\":0.95},{\"statement\":\"Compare the two manifestations of righteousness—the gift received by grace through faith and the harvest of righteousness that grows through visible works—and analyze how the David analogy distinguishes standing in faith before God from showing works before people.\",\"verb\":\"compare\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"8324c242-533b-726a-9458-03cf5d83458a\",\"edf97ec5-6993-78af-8f09-fc6f0892a758\",\"a62601c8-062f-7006-b0ca-b4c236e7ea47\",\"fb4cfa61-881b-78f2-8173-853f0e169c5b\"],\"confidence\":0.95},{\"statement\":\"Describe generosity as a willing overflow of spiritual righteousness rather than forced compliance, distinguishing a cheerful bountiful sower from one who sows sparingly out of reluctant compulsion.\",\"verb\":\"describe\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"66522a60-bc03-7abf-8434-23545728a3ae\"],\"confidence\":0.92},{\"statement\":\"Analyze the Hebrew concept of Tzedakah by identifying its three ramifications—personal morality, justice, and charity—and evaluate how this fused understanding reframes giving to the poor as a matter of justice rather than optional benevolence.\",\"verb\":\"analyse\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"ca763446-f8c9-7a62-b9c7-2a09335682b3\",\"ac2e0a05-29b4-74c8-a832-f25b79a51268\",\"168b403a-2303-7e1a-ae75-b2ebe56da6b2\",\"0f6e5794-b307-734e-83ba-78fb071fdb2c\"],\"confidence\":0.94},{\"statement\":\"Identify the consecrated financial laws of Kingdom economics—fairness over legal rights, periodic debt cancellation, leaving gleanings, prompt payment of workers, and refusing to exploit desperation—and explain how they contradict self-serving worldly models.\",\"verb\":\"identify\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"564578eb-71d4-7e3e-8488-3848c22e28c8\",\"18fc39b0-81c3-7","2c2-97bd-acc6f572db4e\",\"0b868713-69cd-771a-878c-1eea34533435\",\"430ee9e8-8b9d-7adf-be71-d40305e43624\",\"4e2a0f33-eea5-7122-b69a-0bff630089a2\",\"27e07c83-25f3-71f7-8ec7-7c49dac6fa11\"],\"confidence\":0.93},{\"statement\":\"Apply the two core stewardship truths—that God gives the power to get wealth and demands accountability—to the five pillars of financial faithfulness: budgeting, protection, savings, investment, and debt management.\",\"verb\":\"apply\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"eb6a2bc7-bdc4-7678-a65e-be6523f45587\",\"b4cbbbae-9d05-7bca-bf3e-c383435f4f24\",\"0ea74d78-5376-73c9-8272-67103c85ee27\",\"39e85a0e-0674-7710-9ccd-11af0584acb1\",\"8f73b954-1975-7d2b-9d0c-3d52bd391c17\",\"b6f0551f-99f8-70d8-8e18-9a1e94b37d5c\",\"1a8d6676-5ec6-71b4-9da9-dd3af6eb43a5\",\"570c784d-effb-7201-82f2-0a352c7a5ed0\",\"e75364ba-f2b4-78fa-af21-14317c58ab3f\"],\"confidence\":0.9}],\"keyConcepts\":[{\"text\":\"Anchor promise in Proverbs 8: enduring riches and righteousness are joined to walking in justice\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"8002a06a-c3ea-73c3-a83e-4caa9d2ccbc3\"]},{\"text\":\"Two manifestations of righteousness: positional gift by grace versus practical harvest of works\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"8324c242-533b-726a-9458-03cf5d83458a\",\"a62601c8-062f-7006-b0ca-b4c236e7ea47\"]},{\"text\":\"The David analogy: faith and covenant before God, visible evidence of works before people\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"fb4cfa61-881b-78f2-8173-853f0e169c5b\"]},{\"text\":\"Generosity as cheerful overflow of righteousness; sowing sparingly reflects the heart's compulsion\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"66522a60-bc03-7abf-8434-23545728a3ae\"]},{\"text\":\"Tzedakah: Hebrew fusion of morality, justice, and charity where giving to the poor is justice\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"ca763446-f8c9-7a62-b9c7-2a09335682b3\",\"0f6e5794-b307-734e-83ba-78fb071fdb2c\"]},{\"text\":\"Kingdom economics: consecrated laws (returned collateral, debt cancellation, gleanings, prompt wages, no exploitation) that oppose worldly models\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"564578eb-71d4-7e3e-8488-3848c22e28c8\",\"18fc39b0-81c3-72c2-97bd-acc6f572db4e\",","\"0b868713-69cd-771a-878c-1eea34533435\",\"430ee9e8-8b9d-7adf-be71-d40305e43624\",\"4e2a0f33-eea5-7122-b69a-0bff630089a2\",\"27e07c83-25f3-71f7-8ec7-7c49dac6fa11\"]},{\"text\":\"Stewardship truths: God gives the power to get wealth; believers are managers, not owners, and are accountable\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"eb6a2bc7-bdc4-7678-a65e-be6523f45587\",\"b4cbbbae-9d05-7bca-bf3e-c383435f4f24\",\"0ea74d78-5376-73c9-8272-67103c85ee27\"]},{\"text\":\"Five pillars of financial faithfulness: budgeting/tracking, protection, savings, investment, debt management\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"39e85a0e-0674-7710-9ccd-11af0584acb1\",\"8f73b954-1975-7d2b-9d0c-3d52bd391c17\",\"b6f0551f-99f8-70d8-8e18-9a1e94b37d5c\",\"1a8d6676-5ec6-71b4-9da9-dd3af6eb43a5\",\"570c784d-effb-7201-82f2-0a352c7a5ed0\",\"e75364ba-f2b4-78fa-af21-14317c58ab3f\"]}],\"prerequisiteKnowledge\":[{\"text\":\"Familiarity with basic biblical figures and narratives referenced (Abraham, Moses and Jethro, David and Goliath, Jesus raising Jairus's daughter)\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"fb4cfa61-881b-78f2-8173-853f0e169c5b\",\"f7694cab-eff1-7b2c-9525-d6221224b7ed\",\"e8980c9c-16ee-7561-86b3-18eff76a30cc\"]},{\"text\":\"Working knowledge of common financial terms such as budgeting, savings, insurance, investment, and debt\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"8f73b954-1975-7d2b-9d0c-3d52bd391c17\",\"570c784d-effb-7201-82f2-0a352c7a5ed0\",\"e75364ba-f2b4-78fa-af21-14317c58ab3f\"]},{\"text\":\"Basic understanding that the Bible contains both Old Testament law and New Testament teaching used to frame financial ethics\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"0b868713-69cd-771a-878c-1eea34533435\",\"4e2a0f33-eea5-7122-b69a-0bff630089a2\"]}],\"vocabulary\":[{\"term\":\"Positional righteousness (gift)\",\"definition\":\"The fixed legal credit of righteousness received entirely by grace through faith, apart from works, establishing permanent covenant standing with God.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"8324c242-533b-726a-9458-03cf5d83458a\"]},{\"term\":\"Harvest of righteousness (practical righteousness)\",\"definition\":\"The dynamic, multipliable manifestation of righteou","sness shown through visible fruits and works before people, based on 2 Corinthians 9:10.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"8324c242-533b-726a-9458-03cf5d83458a\",\"edf97ec5-6993-78af-8f09-fc6f0892a758\"]},{\"term\":\"Sowing sparingly\",\"definition\":\"Giving out of reluctant compulsion or exhaustion, lacking excitement or love—a condition of the giver's heart, not merely the amount given.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"66522a60-bc03-7abf-8434-23545728a3ae\"]},{\"term\":\"Tzedakah\",\"definition\":\"The Hebrew word uniting personal morality, justice, and charity into one whole, in which giving to the poor is classified as justice, not optional benevolence.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"ca763446-f8c9-7a62-b9c7-2a09335682b3\",\"0f6e5794-b307-734e-83ba-78fb071fdb2c\"]},{\"term\":\"Gleanings\",\"definition\":\"The corners and unharvested produce business owners were commanded to leave for the poor, the widow, and the stranger—a safety net built into profit-generating activity.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"430ee9e8-8b9d-7adf-be71-d40305e43624\"]},{\"term\":\"Jubilee / periodic debt cancellation\",\"definition\":\"The Old Testament cycle in which debts were canceled every seven years, with lenders warned not to withhold help as the cancellation year approached.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"0b868713-69cd-771a-878c-1eea34533435\"]},{\"term\":\"Stewardship\",\"definition\":\"Managing resources as God's property rather than as an independent owner, with accountability expected regardless of the amount entrusted.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"b4cbbbae-9d05-7bca-bf3e-c383435f4f24\",\"0ea74d78-5376-73c9-8272-67103c85ee27\"]},{\"term\":\"50/30/20 allocation rule\",\"definition\":\"A budgeting formula directing 50% of income to needs, 30% to wants, and 20% to savings and investment, with the savings share rising as income grows.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"a6dfb38a-faba-7987-a0c1-188fc688edb5\",\"995877ef-f92f-7ff6-939d-f8e4e56b466b\",\"1ce650a8-d1e0-793e-bf98-e7aabea9c43c\",\"da01ed2c-677a-7269-b1d8-085a8031c780\"]},{\"term\":\"Emergency fund\",\"definition\":\"A liquid reserve of three to six months of living expen","ses that protects long-term investments from being broken during crises.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"a5ca0409-5df5-7364-88b5-465733a983af\"]}],\"misconceptions\":[{\"misconception\":\"Righteousness either comes by works or excludes works entirely—so giving and good deeds are irrelevant to it.\",\"correction\":\"Righteousness as a gift is received by grace through faith and cannot increase, but the harvest of righteousness can and should be multiplied through visible works; works do not qualify us before God, yet they demonstrate faith before people.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"8324c242-533b-726a-9458-03cf5d83458a\",\"a62601c8-062f-7006-b0ca-b4c236e7ea47\"]},{\"misconception\":\"Giving to the poor is optional benevolence that generous people may choose.\",\"correction\":\"In Tzedakah, giving to the poor is classified as justice and righteousness; withholding help when you have power to give violates it.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"0f6e5794-b307-734e-83ba-78fb071fdb2c\"]},{\"misconception\":\"'Sowing sparingly' simply means giving a small amount of money.\",\"correction\":\"Sowing sparingly describes the heart state—giving out of reluctant compulsion or exhaustion—not merely the financial quantity.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"66522a60-bc03-7abf-8434-23545728a3ae\"]},{\"misconception\":\"Exercising a legal right over a debtor is always acceptable in business.\",\"correction\":\"Biblical law required returning a poor debtor's cloak before sundown; legal right must never supersede basic humanity and fairness.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"18fc39b0-81c3-72c2-97bd-acc6f572db4e\"]},{\"misconception\":\"Buying an asset extremely cheaply from a desperate seller is just smart negotiating.\",\"correction\":\"Believers must never monetize another's desperation; oppressing the afflicted prompts the Lord to plead their cause and plunder the plunderers.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"27e07c83-25f3-71f7-8ec7-7c49dac6fa11\"]},{\"misconception\":\"A larger income will automatically solve financial problems.\",\"correction\":\"Your current financial level is a stewardship test; if you can","not manage 200,000 naira, 20 million will only enable more expensive mistakes.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"0ea74d78-5376-73c9-8272-67103c85ee27\"]},{\"misconception\":\"Spiritual power or divine blessing alone is enough to sustain finances without practical planning.\",\"correction\":\"Power produces the miracle but wisdom sustains it—Moses needed Jethro's systems, and Jesus ordered food for the girl He raised; practical wisdom must follow blessing.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"f7694cab-eff1-7b2c-9525-d6221224b7ed\",\"8072ae74-8c46-71f3-90ea-2706ca73e3c6\",\"e8980c9c-16ee-7561-86b3-18eff76a30cc\"]}],\"assessmentQuestions\":[{\"question\":\"Using Proverbs 8:18-21, explain how enduring riches are connected to righteousness and justice, and what this implies about how believers should pursue wealth.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"8002a06a-c3ea-73c3-a83e-4caa9d2ccbc3\"]},{\"question\":\"Compare righteousness as a gift with the harvest of righteousness, citing the scriptures used in the teaching, and explain why both must be active in a believer's life.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"8324c242-533b-726a-9458-03cf5d83458a\",\"edf97ec5-6993-78af-8f09-fc6f0892a758\"]},{\"question\":\"In the David analogy, what would David say to Goliath versus to King Saul, and what does this teach about faith before God and works before people?\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"fb4cfa61-881b-78f2-8173-853f0e169c5b\"]},{\"question\":\"What does 'sowing sparingly' actually describe, and how does a bountiful sower's attitude differ?\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"66522a60-bc03-7abf-8434-23545728a3ae\"]},{\"question\":\"List the three ramifications of Tzedakah and explain why withholding help from the poor is treated as injustice.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"ca763446-f8c9-7a62-b9c7-2a09335682b3\",\"ac2e0a05-29b4-74c8-a832-f25b79a51268\",\"168b403a-2303-7e1a-ae75-b2ebe56da6b2\",\"0f6e5794-b307-734e-83ba-78fb071fdb2c\"]},{\"question\":\"Identify at least three laws of Kingdom economics from the teaching and explain how each contradicts self-serving worldly business models.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"564578eb-71d4-7e3e-","8488-3848c22e28c8\",\"18fc39b0-81c3-72c2-97bd-acc6f572db4e\",\"430ee9e8-8b9d-7adf-be71-d40305e43624\",\"4e2a0f33-eea5-7122-b69a-0bff630089a2\",\"27e07c83-25f3-71f7-8ec7-7c49dac6fa11\"]},{\"question\":\"State the two core truths of financial stewardship and describe how each of the five pillars puts those truths into practice.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"eb6a2bc7-bdc4-7678-a65e-be6523f45587\",\"0ea74d78-5376-73c9-8272-67103c85ee27\",\"39e85a0e-0674-7710-9ccd-11af0584acb1\",\"8f73b954-1975-7d2b-9d0c-3d52bd391c17\",\"b6f0551f-99f8-70d8-8e18-9a1e94b37d5c\",\"1a8d6676-5ec6-71b4-9da9-dd3af6eb43a5\",\"570c784d-effb-7201-82f2-0a352c7a5ed0\",\"e75364ba-f2b4-78fa-af21-14317c58ab3f\"]}],\"focusCoverage\":{\"status\":\"covered\"}}"],"textChunksTruncated":false,"textCharacters":12687,"reasoningCharacters":0,"finishReason":"stop","inputTokens":"[REDACTED]","outputTokens":"[REDACTED]"},"retries":0,"latencyMs":33123,"service":"pipeline-worker","correlationId":"01a0f837-11f4-7327-b2e1-c70e2e9ecef6"}}
