nguish between positional righteousness (the gift received by grace through faith, fixed and perfect, based on Galatians 3:6 and Romans 4) and the harvest of righteousness (practical, agricultural, and capable of multiplication, based on 2 Corinthians 9:10). Emphasize that while the gift establishes permanent standing, the harvest produces visible fruit.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a0f837-810c-7c8b-b238-c3abe72186b5\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"8324c242-533b-726a-9458-03cf5d83458a\", \"edf97ec5-699","3-78af-8f09-fc6f0892a758\", \"a62601c8-062f-7006-b0ca-b4c236e7ea47\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 40\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"analogy\",\n      \"title\": \"The David Test: Standing Before God vs. Showing Before People\",\n      \"description\": \"Use the David and Goliath narrative to illustrate how we present different credentials depending on the audience. Before God (Goliath), we stand on covenant faith and Christ's finished work ('You dare defy the armies of the living God?'). Before people (King Saul), we must show tangible evidence and works ('I have killed a lion and a bear'). This clarifies how faith and works operate in distinct spheres.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a0f837-810c-7c8b-b238-c3abe72186b5\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"fb4cfa61-881b-78f2-8173-853f0e169c5b\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 35\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Generosity as Willing Overflow\",\n      \"description\": \"Contrast the bountiful sower with one who sows sparingly. Drawing from 2 Corinthians 9, explain that true generosity is not forced compliance or a compliance gimmick, but a natural, willing overflow of spiritual righteousness. Sowing sparingly describes a heart condition of reluctant compulsion and exhaustion, while bountiful sowing flows from divine contentment ('godliness with contentment is great gain').\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a0f837-810c-7adc-85d0-888311cb031f\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"66522a60-bc03-7abf-8434-23545728a3ae\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 30\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Tzedakah: The Threefold Nature of Righteousness\",\n      \"description\": \"Unpack the Hebrew concept of Tzedakah, which fuses what English splits into separate categories. Detail the three ramifications: personal morality (internal rectitude), justice (structural fairness in society), and charity/generosity. Emphasize that giving to the poor is not optional benevolence but a matter of justice—to withhold help when able is to violate Tzedakah.\",\n      \"object","iveIds\": [\"01a0f837-810c-7ccf-8992-5e47be7b8c4f\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ca763446-f8c9-7a62-b9c7-2a09335682b3\", \"ac2e0a05-29b4-74c8-a832-f25b79a51268\", \"168b403a-2303-7e1a-ae75-b2ebe56da6b2\", \"0f6e5794-b307-734e-83ba-78fb071fdb2c\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 35\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Kingdom Economics: Consecrated Financial Laws\",\n      \"description\": \"Survey the five consecrated laws that contradict self-serving worldly models: (1) Fairness over legal rights (returning the debtor's cloak by sundown), (2) Periodic debt cancellation (Jubilee cycle), (3) Leaving gleanings for the poor (building safety nets into business models), (4) Prompt payment of workers (avoiding the woe of Jeremiah 22:13), and (5) Refusing to exploit bargaining power (not monetizing others' desperation).\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a0f837-810c-72fa-b35a-cfe41bd9dba1\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"564578eb-71d4-7e3e-8488-3848c22e28c8\", \"18fc39b0-81c3-72c2-97bd-acc6f572db4e\", \"0b868713-69cd-771a-878c-1eea34533435\", \"430ee9e8-8b9d-7adf-be71-d40305e43624\", \"4e2a0f33-eea5-7122-b69a-0bff630089a2\", \"27e07c83-25f3-71f7-8ec7-7c49dac6fa11\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 35\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Stewardship Truths and the Five Pillars\",\n      \"description\": \"Present the two core stewardship truths: (1) God gives the power to get wealth (Deuteronomy 8:18), making us managers rather than owners, and (2) God demands accountability for growth (Parable of the Talents), meaning faithfulness is expected regardless of the amount entrusted. Apply these to the five pillars of financial faithfulness: budgeting/tracking, protection, savings, investment, and debt management.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a0f837-810c-7318-94aa-74783173a067\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"eb6a2bc7-bdc4-7678-a65e-be6523f45587\", \"b4cbbbae-9d05-7bca-bf3e-c383435f4f24\", \"0ea74d78-5376-73c9-8272-67103c85ee27\", \"39e85a0e-0674-7710-9ccd-11af0584acb1\", \"8f73b954-1975-7d2b-9d0c-3d52bd391c17","\", \"b6f0551f-99f8-70d8-8e18-9a1e94b37d5c\", \"1a8d6676-5ec6-71b4-9da9-dd3af6eb43a5\", \"570c784d-effb-7201-82f2-0a352c7a5ed0\", \"e75364ba-f2b4-78fa-af21-14317c58ab3f\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 40\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"summary\",\n      \"title\": \"Integrating Righteousness and Resources\",\n      \"description\": \"Synthesize the teaching by reaffirming that true riches flow from walking in Tzedakah—where morality, justice, and generosity are inseparable. Righteousness is both a gift received by faith and a harvest multiplied through works. Generosity is the cheerful overflow of this righteousness, and financial stewardship is the practical management of God's resources according to Kingdom laws that prioritize justice over profit.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a0f837-810c-764c-a50a-1901bf0ad6de\", \"01a0f837-810c-7c8b-b238-c3abe72186b5\", \"01a0f837-810c-7adc-85d0-888311cb031f\", \"01a0f837-810c-7ccf-8992-5e47be7b8c4f\", \"01a0f837-810c-72fa-b35a-cfe41bd9dba1\", \"01a0f837-810c-7318-94aa-74783173a067\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"8002a06a-c3ea-73c3-a83e-4caa9d2ccbc3\", \"66522a60-bc03-7abf-8434-23545728a3ae\", \"ca763446-f8c9-7a62-b9c7-2a09335682b3\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 25\n    }\n  ]\n}"],"textChunksTruncated":false,"textCharacters":7188,"reasoningCharacters":0,"finishReason":"stop","inputTokens":"[REDACTED]","outputTokens":"[REDACTED]"},"retries":0,"latencyMs":31419,"service":"pipeline-worker","correlationId":"01a0f837-11f4-7327-b2e1-c70e2e9ecef6"}}
